## PHASE 6 — Update Control Board

Update `ai-dev/<ticket-number>/control.md`:

- Set `Review` status:
  - `done` if verdict is `approved` or `approved-with-comments`
  - `in-progress` if verdict is `changes-requested` (re-run `/review` after fixes)
- Add Decision Log entry with verdict and date

If verdict is `approved` or `approved-with-comments`, also print:
> "✅ Ready to raise PR from `<ticket-number>` → `develop`
> Remember to: squash commits if needed, update PR description with plan.md summary"

---

## PHASE 7 — Re-Review After Fixes

If the developer fixes issues and runs `/review` again on the same ticket:
- Note "Re-review" at the top
- Focus only on previously flagged issues
- Confirm fixes are correct or note if still problematic
- Update verdict accordingly

---

## Error Handling

- If diff is empty: warn "No changes detected on this branch vs develop. Ensure you are on the correct branch."
- If plan.md is missing: proceed with code-only review, note plan is unavailable
- If very large diff (50+ files): prioritise reviewing files listed in development.md, note others were spot-checked only
